Contract: `sumSquares(nums []int) int` should compute the sum of squares concurrently and return the correct total, with no data race under `go test -race`. Does this implementation meet the contract? If not, name the bug and the minimal fix.

```go
func sumSquares(nums []int) int {
    total := 0
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for _, n := range nums {
        wg.Add(1)
        go func(n int) {
            defer wg.Done()
            total += n * n
        }(n)
    }
    wg.Wait()
    return total
}
